edback while summarizing the key points you discussed for his reference.</p=
><h3 data-path-to-node=3D"2">Follow-up Email to Thad</h3><p data-path-to-no=
de=3D"3"><b data-path-to-node=3D"3" data-index-in-node=3D"0">Subject:</b> R=
e: Co-Founder / Chief Operating Officer, OpenWorldTech.io</p><p data-path-t=
o-node=3D"4">Hi Thad,</p><p data-path-to-node=3D"5">Thank you again for the=
 time this morning. It was an incredibly interesting and enlightening chat=
=E2=80=94I really appreciate you sharing your perspective on the current ve=
nture landscape and being so candid with your feedback on our current posit=
ioning.</p><p data-path-to-node=3D"6">As I mentioned, I=E2=80=99m jumping i=
nto the deep end on the corporate/fundraising side, so having a "pilot" wit=
h your experience to help navigate these waters is exactly what I'm looking=
 for. I jotted down a few of the main points from our call for reference as=
 we both consider the next steps:</p><ul data-path-to-node=3D"7"><li><p dat=
a-path-to-node=3D"7,0,0"><b data-path-to-node=3D"7,0,0" data-index-in-node=
=3D"0">Fundraising Calibration:</b> You noted that our current $1M target i=
s likely too low for the runway required in the current AI market. A $3M pr=
e-seed round is a more realistic "market-palpable" target to ensure we hit =
the necessary milestones for a Series A.</p></li><li><p data-path-to-node=
=3D"7,1,0"><b data-path-to-node=3D"7,1,0" data-index-in-node=3D"0">Cap Tabl=
e &amp; Valuation:</b> We discussed tightening the caps to ensure I don=E2=
=80=99t get "washed out" too early. Keeping founder ownership high (70-80% =
pre-Series A) is a priority for investor stability and my own long-term con=
trol.</p></li><li><p data-path-to-node=3D"7,2,0"><b data-path-to-node=3D"7,=
2,0" data-index-in-node=3D"0">Revenue Projections:</b> My initial $700k Yea=
r 2 projection is too conservative for VCs looking for a unicorn trajectory=
. We need to model for a more aggressive "scale-up" narrative (e.g., $1M Ye=
ar 1 / $5M Year 2) to demonstrate the true market potential.</p></li><li><p=
 data-path-to-node=3D"7,3,0"><b data-path-to-node=3D"7,3,0" data-index-in-n=
ode=3D"0">Pitch Deck Refinement:</b> The deck needs to be less "global" and=
 more specific. We need to lead with the immediate problem (AI usability/in=
tegration) and the specific "initial market" we are capturing before talkin=
g about the broader ecosystem.</p></li><li><p data-path-to-node=3D"7,4,0"><=
b data-path-to-node=3D"7,4,0" data-index-in-node=3D"0">Operational Path:</b=
> We discussed the possibility of an Advisory Board role (5-10 hours/week) =
vs. a full-time COO. This would allow us to leverage your network and exper=
ience to close the seed round while the product is still in the "build" pha=
se.</p></li></ul><p data-path-to-node=3D"8">I=E2=80=99m really encouraged b=
y your interest in the vision and your philosophy of "decisions in the best=
 interest of the company." I=E2=80=99ll look forward to hearing your though=
ts in a few days once you=E2=80=99ve had a chance to digest everything.</p>=
