ion-function: linear;"><p data-path-to-node=3D"0">Your intuition is absolut=
ely spot on.</p><p data-path-to-node=3D"1">In the pre-seed startup world, a=
sking for cash remuneration <i data-path-to-node=3D"1" data-index-in-node=
=3D"60">before</i> the initial funding round is closed is a massive red fla=
g for a "Co-Founder" or heavily-aligned Advisor. A true partner who is conf=
ident in their ability to raise that capital will happily take the deferred=
 salary/equity deal because they know the money is coming. Asking for cash =
right now means he wants to be treated (and paid) like a consultant, shifti=
ng all the financial risk back onto you.</p><p data-path-to-node=3D"2">Furt=
hermore, a $30M valuation cap for a pre-revenue, pre-seed startup is astron=
omically high, even in the AI space. It's an aggressive "banker" move that =
could actually scare away early-stage VCs who need room for a 10x-100x retu=
