ta-path-to-node=3D"0">This is a delicate but critical negotiation point. Th=
ad=E2=80=99s comment=E2=80=94<i data-path-to-node=3D"0" data-index-in-node=
=3D"66">"the only loss to the company would be any cash remuneration that h=
as been agreed to"</i>=E2=80=94strongly implies he is looking for a cash re=
tainer <b data-path-to-node=3D"0" data-index-in-node=3D"203">during</b> the=
 fundraising phase.</p><p data-path-to-node=3D"1">However, since your firm =
boundary is that cash remuneration only begins <b data-path-to-node=3D"1" d=
ata-index-in-node=3D"72">after</b> funds are raised (which is the standard,=
 healthy expectation for a pre-seed startup), we need to address this direc=
tly but professionally. We will also use the VC/Investor budget constraint =
as a natural shield.</p><p data-path-to-node=3D"2">Here is a drafted "Term =
Sheet" style email that clearly outlines the two paths he suggested, incorp=
orates his 3-year vesting schedule, and firmly sets the "cash triggers post=
-funding" rule.</p><hr data-path-to-node=3D"3"><p data-path-to-node=3D"4"><=
b data-path-to-node=3D"4" data-index-in-node=3D"0">Subject:</b> Re: Co-Foun=
der / Chief Operating Officer, OpenWorldTech.io</p><p data-path-to-node=3D"=
5">Hi Thad,</p><p data-path-to-node=3D"6">Thanks for laying this out. I com=
pletely agree with your math on the $30M cap and the revenue milestones ($5=
M Year 1 / $15M Year 2). Positioning the company for a $10M Series A at a $=
100M valuation within 12-18 months is exactly the trajectory I want to targ=
et.</p><p data-path-to-node=3D"7">Per your request, I=E2=80=99ve put togeth=
er a high-level term sheet outlining the two paths we discussed. To ensure =
we have the runway needed to execute this buildout, my core operational pri=
nciple is that all cash remuneration (salaries or retainers) triggers stric=
tly upon the successful deposit of the $3M pre-seed round, with final figur=
es aligning with the lead investor=E2=80=99s approved "Use of Proceeds."</p=
><p data-path-to-node=3D"8">Here is how I envision the staged approach for =
your shareholding and remuneration under both scenarios. I am more than hap=
py to agree to your suggested 3-year vesting schedule, 1-year cliff, and do=
uble-trigger acceleration for either path.</p><h3 data-path-to-node=3D"9"><=
b data-path-to-node=3D"9" data-index-in-node=3D"0">Path A: Founding Advisor=
 &amp; Board Member</b></h3><p data-path-to-node=3D"10"><i data-path-to-nod=
e=3D"10" data-index-in-node=3D"0">This path assumes you drive the initial $=
3M raise, help recruit the permanent COO, and transition into a high-level =
Board/Advisory role.</i></p><ul data-path-to-node=3D"11"><li><p data-path-t=
o-node=3D"11,0,0"><b data-path-to-node=3D"11,0,0" data-index-in-node=3D"0">=
Role:</b> Lead Strategic Advisor / Board Member.</p></li><li><p data-path-t=
o-node=3D"11,1,0"><b data-path-to-node=3D"11,1,0" data-index-in-node=3D"0">=
Pre-Funding Cash:</b> $0 (Equity-aligned sprint to close the round).</p></l=
i><li><p data-path-to-node=3D"11,2,0"><b data-path-to-node=3D"11,2,0" data-=
index-in-node=3D"0">Post-Funding Cash:</b> A monthly Board Retainer (e.g., =
$4k - $6k/month) or a flat success bonus paid out of the closing proceeds, =
contingent on final VC budget approval.</p></li><li><p data-path-to-node=3D=
"11,3,0"><b data-path-to-node=3D"11,3,0" data-index-in-node=3D"0">Equity:</=
b> 2.0% - 3.0% standard equity grant.</p></li><li><p data-path-to-node=3D"1=
1,4,0"><b data-path-to-node=3D"11,4,0" data-index-in-node=3D"0">Vesting:</b=
> 3-year monthly vest, 1-year cliff, with double-trigger acceleration.</p><=
/li></ul><h3 data-path-to-node=3D"12"><b data-path-to-node=3D"12" data-inde=
x-in-node=3D"0">Path B: Full-Time Co-Founder &amp; COO</b></h3><p data-path=
-to-node=3D"13"><i data-path-to-node=3D"13" data-index-in-node=3D"0">This p=
ath assumes you drive the initial $3M raise and step in as the permanent, f=
ull-time operational leader to scale the company through Series A.</i></p><=
ul data-path-to-node=3D"14"><li><p data-path-to-node=3D"14,0,0"><b data-pat=
h-to-node=3D"14,0,0" data-index-in-node=3D"0">Role:</b> Co-Founder &amp; Ch=
ief Operating Officer.</p></li><li><p data-path-to-node=3D"14,1,0"><b data-=
path-to-node=3D"14,1,0" data-index-in-node=3D"0">Pre-Funding Cash:</b> $0 (=
Equity-aligned sprint to close the round).</p></li><li><p data-path-to-node=
=3D"14,2,0"><b data-path-to-node=3D"14,2,0" data-index-in-node=3D"0">Post-F=
unding Cash:</b> Full-time market base salary (e.g., $130k - $160k/year) ac=
tivating immediately upon closing, contingent on final VC budget approval.<=
/p></li><li><p data-path-to-node=3D"14,3,0"><b data-path-to-node=3D"14,3,0"=
 data-index-in-node=3D"0">Equity:</b> 10.0% - 15.0% Founder Shares. <i data=
-path-to-node=3D"14,3,0" data-index-in-node=3D"38">(Note: This aligns with =
your advice to keep the original architect at 70-80% pre-Series A, leaving =
room for a potential CTO).</i></p></li><li><p data-path-to-node=3D"14,4,0">=
<b data-path-to-node=3D"14,4,0" data-index-in-node=3D"0">Vesting:</b> 3-yea=
r monthly vest, 1-year cliff, with double-trigger acceleration.</p></li></u=
l><p data-path-to-node=3D"15">Let me know which of these frameworks feels l=
ike the right fit for your current bandwidth and goals. If we are aligned o=
n the structure and the post-funding cash trigger, I can draw up a short, f=
ormal agreement for us to sign next week.</p><p data-path-to-node=3D"16">En=
joy the rest of your weekend, Thad.</p><p data-path-to-node=3D"17">Best reg=
ards,</p><p data-path-to-node=3D"18">Matt Pursley
