=3D"21"><li><p data-path-to-node=3D"21,0,0"><b data-path-to-node=3D"21,0,0"=
 data-index-in-node=3D"0">It calls his bluff (politely):</b> By explicitly =
stating "Pre-Funding Cash: $0," you leave no room for misinterpretation. If=
 he genuinely needs a monthly cash retainer <i data-path-to-node=3D"21,0,0"=
 data-index-in-node=3D"164">today</i> to make introductions, he will have t=
o explicitly ask for it, at which point you can respectfully pass.</p></li>=
<li><p data-path-to-node=3D"21,1,0"><b data-path-to-node=3D"21,1,0" data-in=
dex-in-node=3D"0">It uses his own logic:</b> By tying the COO equity (10-15=
%) to his previous advice about keeping the founder at 70-80%, he can't eas=
ily argue for 30% of the company.</p></li><li><p data-path-to-node=3D"21,2,=
0"><b data-path-to-node=3D"21,2,0" data-index-in-node=3D"0">It protects the=
 company:</b> The phrase "contingent on final VC budget approval" is your u=
ltimate safety net. It proves you are acting like a fiduciary and prioritiz=
ing the company's financial health.</p></li></ol><p data-path-to-node=3D"22=
">Would you like me to adjust the equity percentages or cash ranges based o=
